id: DRAFT-glob-0.0.1-cmake-offline-install
severity: 2
category: build-system|cmake|conan|offline-build
trigger_tool: cmake|conan|CPM.cmake|PackageProject.cmake
phase: configure|build|package
approach: remove-network-fetch-add-install-rules
keywords: CPM.cmake, PackageProject.cmake, configure-time download, offline Conan, CMake install, static library
error_signature: Could not download CPM.cmake or PackageProject.cmake during CMake configure
match_keywords: CPMAddPackage,PackageProject.cmake,configure-time,offline,install(TARGETS
title: Offline Conan packaging for CMake projects that fetch PackageProject at configure time
root_cause: Upstream CMake projects may fetch CPM/PackageProject helper modules during configure and may only define a build target without install rules. This makes an otherwise dependency-free library fail in offline CI and leaves Conan package() with no portable artifact boundary.
affected_scope: CMake libraries using CPM/FetchContent helper downloads at configure time and lacking explicit install rules.
verification_cmd: conan create <archive> -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<ohos-profile> --build=missing; test_package must link and execute a real API consumer.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: replace-network-helper-with-explicit-install
rec_description: Remove configure-time helper downloads when they are only used to install/package the library; declare a static or shared target explicitly, add GNUInstallDirs install(TARGETS) and install(DIRECTORY) rules, then let Conan CMake.install() package the resulting files.
rec_command: include(GNUInstallDirs); install(TARGETS <target> ARCHIVE DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}); install(DIRECTORY include/ DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR})
rec_auto_fix: false
forbid_1_pattern: CPMAddPackage.*PackageProject
forbid_1_reason: Configure-time GitHub fetches are not reproducible in offline CI and can fail before the compiler is invoked.
forbid_1_consequence: Conan create fails during CMake configure even when the library itself has no external runtime dependencies.
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: vendor-helper-or-provide-local-cache
fallback_description: If the helper supplies functionality beyond installation, vendor a pinned copy or provide a controlled local source; do not silently re-enable an unpinned network fetch.
fallback_command: use a pinned helper under cmake/ or an explicit Conan build requirement
fallback_auto_fix: false
